<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-AA-</p>
<p>The Chugoku Electric Power Co Inc, 35 billion yen mortgaged due 2003.</p>
<p>Osaka Gas Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2000.</p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Toshiba Co, 30 billion yen unsecured due 2000.  </p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Tsuzuki Densan Co Ltd, 25 million Swiss Francs unsecured with warrants due 2001, private placement, guaranteed by Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank.</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Ibiden Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2005.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi Chemical Corp,</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2003</p>
<p>10 billion yen unseucred due 2007.</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2009.  </p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Kasumi Co Ltd, five billion yen unsecured due 2004.</p>
<p>Orix Corp, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2009.</p>
<p>-CCC-</p>
<p>Meitetsu Transport Co Ltd, three billion yen unsecured due 2003.</p>
</text>
